**《張釋之馮唐列傳》**  
Zhang Jie, who was a magistrate of堵阳, was also named Zhuge Ji. He had a brother, Zhong Tong, who lived with him. Because he was a minor, he did not have any reputation.  
Zhuge Jie said, "Long-term service reduces the production of his brother, and I cannot succeed." He wanted to avoid being exiled.  
The Minister of Military Affairs, Yan Gu, knew he was a good man, but was sad about his departure. He asked to transfer him to the position of a porter.  
Zhuge Jie went to court, and then made a suggestion about beneficial matters. Emperor Wen of Han said, "Don't be too high in criticism; let it be done now."  
At that time, Zhuge Jie spoke about matters in the Han and Qin eras, which had been lost to the Han and gained by the Han. Emperor Wen of Han praised him, and he was appointed as a porter's supervisor.  
Zhuge Jie went on to say, "How do you view the Emperor of Zhou? The Emperor of Zhou is a great man." Emperor Wen of Han replied, "A great man." He then asked, "How do you view the Duke of East and Yang?" Emperor Wen of Han said, "A great man."  
Zhuge Jie said, "The Emperor of Zhou and the Duke of East are called great men, but they cannot speak or express their opinions. How can a porter be so skilled at speaking and winning arguments?"  
Furthermore, the Han used officials who were responsible for writing and copying, and they were criticized for being too fast and strict. However, the burden fell on the people who were honest and diligent. Therefore, they did not hear about their faults and were not punished.  
At that time, the Han court was in turmoil. Emperor Wen of Han said, "The porter spoke and was promoted, but I fear the world will follow the wind and become chaotic. If the porter speaks and is promoted, the world will become chaotic. Moreover, the lower classes are in the fast of the upper classes, and the judgment cannot be made without careful consideration."  
Emperor Wen of Han said, "That is right." He stopped promoting the porter.  
The Emperor went to the palace, summoned Zhuge Jie as his companion, and walked slowly. He asked Zhuge Jie about the Han's corruption.  
Zhuge Jie presented his case. Emperor Wen of Han called him to the palace.  
At that time, the Crown Prince and Liang Wang were together in the palace and went to the court. They did not enter the palace gates, and therefore Zhuge Jie did not allow them to enter the palace.  
He then reported that the porter did not enter the palace gates without respect. He reported it to the Minister of Justice.  
The Minister of Justice, Qin Xian, reported that Zhuge Jie was accused of stealing the imperial throne. Emperor Wen of Han was furious and said, "The people have no right to steal the imperial throne. I am the Minister of Justice. I want to punish them for stealing the throne, but you are not doing it for me. I am not doing it for the imperial throne."  
Zhuge Jie bowed down and bowed down, saying, "The law is so strong that it is enough for me."  
He also blamed others, but with respect to their actions, he did not consider their right or wrong.  
At that time, the Minister of Justice, Qin Xian, and the Crown Prince, Liang Wang, met to discuss Zhuge Jie's case. They agreed to support him.  
After this, the Crown Prince was killed, and the Prince of Liang was killed.  
Zhuge Jie was afraid of death and wanted to be exempted. He was afraid of being executed; he wanted to be exempted.  
He used the plan of the Minister of Justice to get the exemption, but the Prince of Liang did not know how to act.  
Zhuge Jie was a good person who spoke well of the Yellow Emperor. He was a scholar.  
Zhuge Jie had been summoned to the court for a long time, and all the ministers and officials were gathered. Wang Sheng, a scholar, said, "I am the one who understands the meaning of 'Wei'." He told Zhang Jie, "I will help you understand 'Wei'."  
Zhuge Jie bowed down and helped Zhang Jie understand 'Wei'.  
After that, some people said, "Why did Zhang Jie be in the court? Only to insult Zhang Jie, and he bowed down to help him understand 'Wei'."  
Wang Sheng said, "I am old and poor, and I think I will not help Zhang Jie. Zhang Jie is a great man. I am just a little old and poor, and I think I will not help Zhang Jie. Zhang Jie is a great man. I am just a little old and poor, and I think I will not help Zhang Jie."  
